================================================================================
WHY THE DEVELOP LANE
================================================================================

bERP HRMS tracks upstream's develop lane, and this is deliberate. Which bench it
is deliberate FOR is the part to get right.

bERP is assembled two different ways, and this module belongs to one of them.

  The development bench -- where this module is installed

      frappe                    develop (17.0.0-dev)
      erpnext                   bstBizEra/bERP (17.0.0-dev)
      berp_hrms                 THIS repository (17.0.0-dev)
      crm                       bstBizEra/bERP-CRM (17.0.0-dev)
      berp_branding, berp_lao   from bstBizEra/bERP

  Assembled by scripts/install-berp-apps.sh in this repository.

  The tenant bench -- what customers run, and it does NOT hold this module

      frappe                    released version-16
      erpnext                   UPSTREAM frappe/erpnext, released version-16
      hrms                      UPSTREAM frappe/hrms, pinned at version-16
      lending, berp_branding, berp_lao

  Assembled by scripts/deploy/berp_deploy.sh in bstBizEra/bERP, which pins
  upstream hrms in scripts/apps/pins.json. That repository's own
  scripts/deploy/README.md states it plainly: "The ERPNext tree in this
  repository is 17.0.0-dev. The tenants run the released v16 line."

On the development bench, bstBizEra/bERP declares name = "erpnext", so it
occupies the bench's erpnext application slot and requires
frappe >=17.0.0-dev,<18.0.0. This module's frappe >=17.0.0-dev,<18.0.0 and
erpnext >=17.0.0-dev,<18.0.0 match it, as does bstBizEra/bERP-CRM.

Upstream's stable lane (version-16, 16.19.0) requires frappe >=16.0.0,<17.0.0
and erpnext >=16.0.0,<17.0.0. bench compares these with semantic_version, and a
`<17.0.0` bound excludes the 17.0.0-dev prerelease, so the stable lane cannot be
installed on that bench while the bERP fork holds the erpnext slot. The develop
lane is what makes this module installable there at all.

Two things follow that are worth stating rather than leaving to be inferred.

This repository is not what a tenant receives today. A tenant's HR module is
upstream frappe/hrms at version-16, and a change made here does not reach a
customer until the platform's tenant line moves to this module.

Until this module was renamed, the two could not even be told apart: both
installed as `hrms`, so no bench could hold them at once. Since the rename they
occupy different application slots -- `berp_hrms` and `hrms` -- and a single
bench can carry both. That is a side effect of the rename rather than its
purpose, and it is not a supported configuration: the two ship the same
doctypes, and installing both on one site would collide on every one of them.

The trade-off of the develop lane is real: this module follows a moving,
unreleased upstream branch and can break when upstream develop moves. That risk
is inherent to the development bench rather than to this module, and it resolves
when the whole bERP stack moves to a released Frappe together.

