================================================================================
MODIFICATIONS FROM UPSTREAM
================================================================================

  Renamed -- the application installs as `berp_hrms`, not as `hrms`:

      The Python package moved from hrms/ to berp_hrms/, and every lowercase
      `hrms` token in the application tree became `berp_hrms`: imports and
      dotted paths, patch paths, /assets/ URLs, desk bundle names, realtime and
      cache keys, the PWA route, and the "app" field on Dock, Desktop Icon,
      Workspace and Sidebar fixtures. Four spellings were deliberately kept --
      github.com/frappe/hrms, the [org_name]/hrms example in config/docs.py, the
      sk_hrms site-config key, and upstream's [frappe.hrms] Crowdin project id.

      app_title became "bERP HR" and app_publisher became bstBizEra. Product
      copy inside the application still reads "Frappe HR" and is unchanged.

      No application logic was modified. Every change is a substitution of the
      package name, and `git log` on any file still shows its upstream
      authorship. The consequence is that `git merge upstream/develop` now
      conflicts across the tree; docs/RENAME_TO_BERP_HRMS.md records the exact
      substitution rule so a sync reproduces it rather than inventing one.

      Two comment-only exceptions: hooks.py and api/oauth.py each carry a
      `# nosemgrep` annotation, because rewriting the package name inside the
      flagged code made two already-triaged inherited findings read as new ones
      to semgrep. docs/SECURITY-BASELINE.md records the exception and why it
      was granted. No executable line changed.

  Added -- deployment and setup tooling, none of which exists upstream:
      scripts/setup-bench.sh          Local bench provisioning
      scripts/install-berp-apps.sh    Shared app assembly: erpnext (bERP),
                                      berp_hrms, crm, berp_branding, berp_lao
      scripts/deploy-dev.sh           Private development VM, reached over SSH
      scripts/deploy-production.sh    Ubuntu 24.04 VM behind nginx with TLS
      berp_hrms/rename_migration.py   In-place hrms -> berp_hrms migration for a
                                      site that already has hrms installed
      berp_hrms/commands.py           Registers `bench rename-from-hrms`, the
                                      only way to reach that migration: bench
                                      execute refuses a dotted path in an app
                                      the site has not installed yet
      docs/LOCAL_SETUP.md
      docs/DEPLOYMENT.md
      docs/DEPLOYMENT_DEV.md
      docs/RENAME_TO_BERP_HRMS.md
      docker/Dockerfile
      .github/workflows/README.md
      NOTICE, docs/SECURITY-BASELINE.md

  Removed -- eight workflows that operated upstream's project rather than this
  one, three of which held contents: write:
      build-and-commit-assets.yml     initiate_release.yml
      build_image.yml                 on_release.yml
      generate-pot-file.yml           release_notes.yml
      review-translation-changes.yaml stale.yml

  Modified:
      .github/helper/install.sh       Resolve upstream dependency branches from
      .github/workflows/patch.yml     this repository's branch names. No upstream
                                      Frappe repository has a `main` branch, so
                                      both map main -> develop. patch.yml
                                      additionally steps its v14 dump up through
                                      UPSTREAM hrms and runs the rename
                                      migration, because the dump is a site with
                                      `hrms` installed.
